TWO THINGS THIS DOES NOT COVER
------------------------------

1. TRANSLATIONS. A translation is a separate copyrightable work with its own
   term. Every Edition record carries its own `license` field with per-
   jurisdiction notes. Public domain is jurisdictional: the King James Version
   remains under perpetual Crown letters patent in the United Kingdom while
   being free elsewhere, and it is recorded that way rather than filed as
   flatly "public domain".

2. COMMENTARY. A fourteenth-century tafsir is public domain; a modern English
   translation of that tafsir is a fresh copyrightable work. Licence is tracked
   per Layer, never per Work.

VERIFICATION
------------

Every TextUnit carries a `provenance` block with a source, a SHA-256 checksum,
and a `verified` flag. Units marked `verified: false` were entered by hand to
demonstrate the data format and are NOT authoritative editions of anyone's
scripture. They must not be displayed to readers. See ../../docs/09-ingestion.md.

